--- Interpretation (C4) ---
--fmad=false is never emitted, so nvcc device codegen ran at its default
--fmad=true for every target. -ffp-contract=off/fast reached the HOST pass only
(nvcc_wrapper routes unrecognized flags via -Xcompiler). Despite that, the two
EFT device-parity passes that were built PASSED with zero failures:
  dd_eft_test  Test D device parity  200000/200000
  ff_eft_test  Test D device parity  400000/400000
So at sm_80 / nvcc 12.9.86 the Dekker twoProduct sequence was NOT contracted
into an FMA in practice. This is an empirical observation for this
compiler+arch, not a guarantee -- the intended guard is still not engaged.
qf_eft_test and all six FMA-guard registrations did not build, so their device
contraction behaviour is UNTESTED.
